  "description": "<div>\n  <p>Directed pair <code>[a,b]</code> says that course <code>a</code> must be taken before <code>b</code>. For each query <code>[a,b]</code>, answer whether a chain of one or more such pairs leads from <code>a</code> to <code>b</code>. Return booleans in the original query order.</p>\n  <p>Only a nonempty chain counts; an ID does not precede itself.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> numCourses = 3, prerequisites = [[0,1],[1,2]], queries = [[0,2],[2,0],[0,1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [true,false,true]</pre>\n  <p>There is a path 0→1→2 but none backward.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> numCourses = 3, prerequisites = [], queries = [[0,1],[1,1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [false,false]</pre>\n  <p>With no edges no course precedes another.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> numCourses = 2, prerequisites = [[0,1]], queries = []\n<strong>Output:</strong> []</pre>\n  <p>There are no questions to answer.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= numCourses &lt;= 100</code>.</li>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= prerequisites.length, queries.length &lt;= 1000</code>; endpoints are valid course IDs.</li>\n    <li>The prerequisite graph has no directed cycles; queries may compare a course with itself, which returns false.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
